local changes, both for zwylib: it names the plugin behind a call by the "ElyxPlugins/<id>/" segment of the path of the
calling file, which is where exteraGram runs the code of an .elyx archive from.
- elyx_runtime/loader.py: the namespace of an archive searches <plugins>/ElyxPlugins/<id>, the link the extraction keeps to
  <plugins>/.elyx_extracted/<id>/<hash>, instead of the hashed folder. without it the entry module of zwylib is src/main.py
  and every setting, async task and hook it registers belongs to a plugin called "main"
- extera_utils/plugin_loader.py: ElyxPlugins joins the markers that give the owner of a file by its path, so the code that
  runs from the link, and a library that neighbours import from there, is still the code of its plugin


local change for the ios 12 sandbox:
- extera_utils/audit_gate.py: _runtime_paths adds every path on its own, as given and resolved, and _is_runtime_file also compares the normalized path as given. one path the sandbox refuses to resolve used to empty the cached list, and a plugin's `import random` was then refused as a file open without the files permission
